hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"246","Bismillahi wallahu Akbar [Allahumma minka wa laka] Allahumma taqabbal minni. In the name of Allah, and Allah is the Greatest [O Allah, from You and to You] O Allah, accept from me"
"247","A'udhu bi-kalimaatillaahit-taam-maatillatee laa yujaawizuhunna barrun wa-laa fajirrun min sharri maa khalaqa wa bara'a wa dhara'a, wa min sharri maa yanzilu minas-samaa'i wa min sharri maa ya'ruju feehaa, wa min sharri maa dhara'a fil-ardhi wa min sharri maa yakhruju minhaa, wa min sharri fitanil-layli wan-nahaar, wa min sharri kulli taa-rin illaa taa-riqun yat-ruqu bi-khayrin yaa Rahmaan.. I seek refuge in the perfect words of Allah, which no righteous or wicked person can surpass, from the evil of what He has created, brought into being, and scattered; from the evil of what descends from the sky and what ascends therein; from the evil of what He has scattered on the earth and what emerges from it; from the evil of the trials of night and day; and from the evil of every visitor, except one who visits with good, O Most Merciful."
